I found a 0:2 /oW at turn 130, so I decided to break the speed record.

The wand went for 3b?C, +2 HOB, +3 jumping boots, bag of holding, and 
(when I had enough HP) the Eye.  I robbed some shops, went down to 
Minetown, gated back to the main dungeon, proceeded down to Sokoban to set 
up a stash, then went down a few more levels till I felt I was ready to 
teleport to the castle.

I came close to beating the castle, but I gated away when a mmf was 
summoned next to me (stupid; I should have dropped my ?oScareMonster).  So 
I wasted some turns in Minetown and then gated back to the castle.  
obtained the wand at turn 3600, a little slower than I would have liked, 
but still good.

Back to Sokoban for some polypiling, but it didn't yield a =oConflict, so 
I finally broke down and wished for it.  My big mistake was not having 
enough polyfodder; I should have done the Valley before proceeding.  So I 
ended up not learning the spell of Magic Mapping, and not noticing until 
much later when I was deep in Gehennom.  

Did the quest (easy).  Gated to the Valley and teleported to the VS level.  
Did Rodney.  Did Vlad.  I still did not have +MagicMapping, but used some 
scrolls I had found.  Did the invocation, started back up.  Wasted at 
least a thousand turns trying to map Gehennom by hand, but did not get 
far.  Finally I spent my final wrest wish on +MagicMapping, and the rest 
of the game was smooth.  I found a marker and magic lamp on the way up but 
didn't use them, although I would have saved some turns if I had.

I had found a HoOA, so I used it on Astral.

